{"engine_version":"0.37.0","file":"campaign-optimize-link-budget.toml","toml":"# An optimisation through a campaign: the link-budget example's X-band link\n# (55 dBW EIRP, 53 dB/K G/T, 3 dB other losses, 4.5 dB required Eb/N0), searched\n# over range and data rate for the operating point that leaves exactly 3 dB of\n# margin. Each evaluation is an ordinary `link-budget` run. The Nelder-Mead simplex\n# works in log-normalised coordinates inside the stated bounds, and every\n# evaluation is listed in the result's `trace`.\n#\n# The margin falls 20 dB per decade of range and 10 dB per decade of data rate, so\n# the 3 dB points form a line across this box. The optimiser returns one point on\n# it, nearest its start; the trace shows the path. Use `method = \"grid\"` with\n# `steps` on each param for an exhaustive search instead.\n#\n# MODELLED: a local search over the box, not a global guarantee, and as good as the\n# `link-budget` kind it runs. Protocol and pre-registered bars:\n# docs/design/evidence/cap32-optimize/.\nkind = \"campaign\"\ntitle = \"Link budget: range and rate for a 3 dB margin\"\nseed = 20261013\n\n[optimize]\nmethod = \"nelder-mead\"\nmax_evals = 300\n\n[optimize.objective]\nname = \"margin\"\npath = \"margin_db\"\ngoal = \"target\"\ntarget = 3.0\n\n[[optimize.params]]\nname = \"range\"\nkey = \"range_km\"\nunit = \"km\"\nlo = 1.0e6\nhi = 1.0e9\nscale = \"log\"\n\n[[optimize.params]]\nname = \"rate\"\nkey = \"data_rate_bps\"\nunit = \"bit/s\"\nlo = 1.0e3\nhi = 1.0e8\nscale = \"log\"\n\n[optimize.scenario]\nkind = \"link-budget\"\nband = \"x\"\neirp_dbw = 55.0\ng_over_t_db = 53.0\nrange_km = 2000.0\ndata_rate_bps = 1.0e6\nother_losses_db = 3.0\nrequired_eb_n0_db = 4.5\n","summary":"campaign f022ad412694 | Link budget: range and rate for a 3 dB margin | optimize `margin` (target 3.0) of `link-budget` by nelder-mead: 177 evals (tolerance), best 3.0 at [range=7.77e7, rate=5.41e5] | 177 member runs (MODELLED)","json":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"0.7\",\n  \